The scalar projection of \(\vec{a}\) onto \(\vec{b}\) is \(\frac{\vec{a}\cdot\vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|}\). Compute \[
\begin{aligned}
\vec{a}\cdot\vec{b}&=2\cdot1+(-1)\cdot2+3\cdot2 \\
&=2-2+6 \\
&=6
\end{aligned}
\]. Also \[
\begin{aligned}
|\vec{b}|&=\sqrt{1^2+2^2+2^2} \\
&=\sqrt{9} \\
&=3
\end{aligned}
\]. Hence the scalar projection is \(\frac{6}{3}=2\). Therefore option B is correct.
